  "worked_solution": "To make our estimation, we proceed as follows:\n\n- We start at $y=4$ on the vertical axis.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944892/assets/19cf6fe36f3afb0322e51ab1d9b1d580453380ba67d813a923818756c1d57994.png)\n\n- Then, we move right until we intersect the trend line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944892/assets/8815a1433c0c139ecf9370da8a6799b084a0e875a3bddb1b80ffa96792c9a145.png)\n\n- Finally, we move down until we intersect the horizontal axis.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944892/assets/f183ff82c15c750d47a0da10151917c02311260f0e86daecfeb1b12c9e15007c.png)\n\nTherefore, these cyclists travel $4$ miles in approximately $20$ minutes.",
